WEBVTT

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:10.030
So this is the Waterfront Area.

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:12.740
There's so much water.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.580
Many aquatic animals live 
in the Waterfront Area.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:22.170
There are also many plants and geographic 
features that match the waterside.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:26.850
Is that where they're holding the concert?

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.790
Must be. I see lots of Friends.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.080
Wow!

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.110
It's so impressive.

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:16.070
What's that, what's that? 
What's that thing do?

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:20.700
Maybe it's the stage that the 
professor and the assistant made?

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.160
What a big crowd of Friends.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.330
Yup, PPP is super popular.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:31.580
Is that another Lucky-san?

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:34.590
Yup. There are lots of them.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.870
Boss, I'm taking two, okay?

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:42.420
You hardly ever see more than one 
Boss in the same place, though.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:43.990
Oh, really?

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:47.140
Today is an exception because of 
the large gathering of Friends.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:51.330
But we can't see the concert with this crowd.

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:54.360
It would be hard to keep 
jumping the whole time.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:17.030
That's it. You're almost there!

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.400
Nice job!

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.370
Kaban-chan, you've gotten 
pretty good at climbing trees.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:30.960
What a great view! Let's watch from here.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.680
We have box seats.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:41.740
Order: Carnivora
Family: Felidae
Genus: Leopardus

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.740
You startled me!

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.900
Who are you two? When did you get there?

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:47.740
You startled us, too.

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.580
Are you here to see PPP, too?

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:53.040
That's right. I couldn't miss their first event.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.920
To think I could watch the third 
generation from their debut...

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.380
I was lucky to be born in this era.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:03.750
If you got here early, 
couldn't you have gotten a closer spot?

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:07.080
Seeing the whole audience 
enriches the experience.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.100
You just don't get it.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.890
What happens next?

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:14.060
Today, there's the official 
unveiling of the new group,

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.120
and an announcement of 
their concert next week.

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:20.530
Every generation of the penguin 
idol unit is hugely popular.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:25.910
But of course they are. 
Girls that cute, singing and dancing...

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.110
It wouldn't make any sense 
if they weren't popular.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:32.380
In fact, the concert tickets 
sold out instantly.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:35.140
Wow, really? We got lucky, then.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:36.290
Yeah, lucky us.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:41.520
Th-That's the one

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:44.860
that includes the concert, handshakes, 
and sitting in on a rehearsal...

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:48.120
A PPP platinum ticket?!

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.570
Where did you get that?!

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.660
From the professor and her assistant.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:55.730
It sounds like it's starting.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:05:01.330
PPP!

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:11.640
Order: Sphenisciformes
Family: Spheniscidae
Genus: Eudyptes

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:11.640
Kept you waiting? 
I'm the Royal Penguin, Princess!

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:15.850
R-Rockhopper Penguin, 
that's me! Rocker for short!

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:15.850
Order: Sphenisciformes
Family: Spheniscidae
Genus: Eudyptes

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:17.470
Gen, you're up!

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:20.320
Order: Sphenisciformes
Family: Spheniscidae
Genus: Pygoscelis

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:21.080
I'm the Gentoo Penguin, Gen! Yes!

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:25.860
Order: Sphenisciformes
Family: Spheniscidae
Genus: Spheniscus

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.010
Hululu!

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.630
Tell them what kind of penguin you are!

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:26.420
Humboldt Penguin.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:29.470
Order: Sphenisciformes
Family: Spheniscidae
Genus: Aptenodytes

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:29.470
I'm the Emperor Penguin... Emperor.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:31.040
And together, we five are...

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:35.310
PPP!

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:50.130
I got stage fright. That sucked!

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:53.740
I wish we had been able to say 
our lines at a better rhythm.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:56.790
It's totally different when we're 
in front of an audience.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:59.580
I couldn't say my part like in rehearsal.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:01.120
That was sloppy!

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:03.420
All of those Friends came to see us.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:05.570
Being an idol means being fun!

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:08.380
Come on, follow Emperor's lead.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.840
She's passed out.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:15.170
Hey, listen.

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:17.770
That round rock thing...

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:21.270
It looked like an egg, didn't it? So cute.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:26.320
Still, we've come a long way.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.900
It wasn't perfect, but we were in front 
of an audience for the first time.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:32.390
Yeah. It's been about a year since that day...

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:36.630
Did any of us think we'd get to be part 
of the legendary penguin idol group?

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:40.500
Singing and dancing turned out 
to be tons of fun, though.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:42.650
I love dancing with you all.

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:44.000
We still have a long way to go!

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:48.260
The first and second generations 
were famous across the whole park.

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:52.550
We'll practice like mad up until the concert, 
and then we'll become legends, too.

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:54.970
Yeah!

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:00.940
No, no! We're not up to par at all!

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:05.520
Gen, you get lost at the "crying and laughing" 
line. Memorize all the choreography!

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:06.440
Got it.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:09.700
Hululu, you're too slow. 
You have to pick up the pace.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:13.080
Rocker, you're rushing too much. 
Watch the rest of us more.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:14.410
Got it.

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.270
And most of all, you're all too stiff.

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:19.250
An idol shouldn't look pained.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:21.970
Thinking about getting it perfect 
only makes you more awkward.

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:23.830
Dance more in the moment!

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:27.560
This is fun and all, 
but being an idol is rough.

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:30.010
The dancing alone is hard enough.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.560
On top of that, we have 
to be cute and showy...

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:36.510
The first generation Emperor's 
dancing was so awe-inspiring.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:39.140
Can I really fill her shoes?

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:41.370
Not to mention... me as the leader?

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:43.980
Wouldn't you make a better leader, Princess?

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:47.610
You should be strong and 
confident, like a leader.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:50.180
I'll back you up with appealing visuals.

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:51.570
Trust me!

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:53.420
You're incredible.

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:56.170
You know the choreography perfectly, 
and you dance with so much energy.

00:07:56.170 --> 00:07:58.530
You have a very beautiful voice, too.

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:01.600
All right! Let's run through it again!

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:02.610
'Scuse me!

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:04.200
Yes?

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:07.500
Is this where we get to do the 
special PPP rehearsal sit-in?

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:11.750
A friend of the professor?

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:15.680
Come in. We owe the professor for 
everything she did to set up this concert.

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:17.010
Yay!

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.520
Nice to meet you. I'm Serval!

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:20.780
I'm Princess.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:23.550
Welcome, and enjoy the rehearsal.

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:26.770
Who's that? More VIP guests?

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.850
Margay, come on in!

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:33.910
G-Give me a minute... I'm so nervous 
about talking to them in person...

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:36.780
Huh? Something smells good...

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:43.670
A-dor-a-ble...

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:45.580
Margay-san!

00:08:46.060 --> 00:09:15.470
Nagoya Aquarium, Touyama Saki-oneesan (Aichi)

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:50.080
They're the only species of Antarctic 
penguins to breed in the winter,

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:53.040
so their bodies need to be 
big enough to endure hunger.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:56.820
They warm their eggs for long periods 
of time without leaving to feed,

00:08:56.820 --> 00:09:00.910
so they need to be big enough to survive 
for a long time without eating.

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:04.200
It's mating season now, and a new 
pair was just recently formed.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:07.750
As they were courting, some 
distance away from the others,

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:10.510
another penguin came charging 
in from fairly far away

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:13.460
and interrupted by hurling itself at them.

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:15.610
I was a bit startled by that.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:19.530
The margay cat is a special, special cat.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:45.410
Belize Zoo, Sharon-oneesan (Belize)

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:24.220
They live all the way up in the treetops, 
and they don't come down to the ground.

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:26.540
They're strictly treetop cats.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:28.900
They eat birds, lizards...

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:32.800
At the zoo, we feed 
our margay cats chicken

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:36.620
and a little beef, and they 
seem very, very happy.

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:40.510
They come up to the fence 
to greet their visitors,

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:45.640
and everybody is always amazed 
at how beautiful the cats are.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:56.310
No, no! We're getting out of sync again!

00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:59.530
This part is the climax. 
We have to be perfectly matched.

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:05.290
I think we've improved a little.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:08.710
But it's nerve-wracking 
in front of an audience.

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:14.130
Right, because everyone expects the 
same quality as the last generation.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:17.310
Don't talk like that. You're 
only gonna psych yourself out.

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:21.280
She's right. Please don't stiffen 
up over your own words.

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:24.160
Anybody have a Japari bun?

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:28.060
Oh, good grief. She's a far cry from nervous...

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:33.520
This is how they interact off-stage...

00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:36.190
They seem close!

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:39.320
And their dancing and singing is fantastic.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:41.410
How'd we do?

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:43.060
You were really great.

00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:43.980
Yes!

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:45.780
That was the best.

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:47.250
The best!

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:51.450
Rocker-san's natural pep! 
That's the Rockhopper position!

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:53.070
A true "Let's rock!"

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:55.310
Gen-san's orthodox idol vibe!

00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:57.260
She's overflowing with 
good sense for the team!

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:59.930
I can't get enough of her 
"I'll do my best!" aura!

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:03.380
Emperor-san's "Am I a good 
enough leader?" aura!

00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:07.680
The difference in flavor from the original 
tickles the heart of the devoted fan!

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:13.650
"Hululu..."-san's airheadedness is essential 
idol material! She soothes the soul!

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:16.740
And most of all, the pillar 
of the group, Princess-san!

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:19.650
In order to bring idols back to the park,

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:21.530
"Work your way up from zero! Have passion!

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:23.210
Practice makes perfect!" A fat-boned...

00:11:23.210 --> 00:11:26.340
I mean, truly a penguin 
with high bone density's...

00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:27.040
Uh.

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:31.210
Who are you? And our voices... 
How can you...

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:33.380
I love my idols!

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:35.750
Wow!

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:40.850
The margay imitates the calls of 
other animals to draw them closer.

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:45.650
That's incredible. I couldn't 
tell the difference.

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:47.930
You know about our predecessors?

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:51.970
I've done a lot of research on them, 
including at the library.

00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:57.110
Each generation is so cool 
and cute. I can't get enough.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:12:00.370
Am I a proper Gen?

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:04.490
Don't worry! The way you're 
so hardworking really resonates.

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:06.600
What was the first generation Rocker like?

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:11.060
Not much different from you. 
You've got it down great.

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:12.620
Awesome!

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:14.180
How do I match up?

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:15.790
What about me?

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:18.220
Okay, okay! Back to rehearsal!

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:20.210
The big day's just around the corner.

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:23.080
Let's keep improving!

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:25.220
Yeah!

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:41.030
I'm getting excited!

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:43.460
The audience is packed.

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:46.530
Let's get fired up!

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:48.540
Make sure the timing of 
the first bars is clean.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:50.700
For the chorus, make sure 
you watch your neighbors.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:51.580
Got it.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:54.090
All right. We've got today in the bag!

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:55.610
Go...

00:12:55.610 --> 00:12:56.280
Now?

00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:58.730
We've got nothing on her.

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:05.860
This is great. They have more volume 
together than when it was only four girls.

00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:10.010
This "Princess-san at the center!" 
feeling is very idol-like!

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:11.350
Four?

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:13.050
It used to be a group of four?

00:13:13.050 --> 00:13:17.220
That's right. PPP's first generation had 
four girls, the second generation had three,

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:19.520
and the third generation has five.

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.570
Then they've powered up!

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:24.530
Huh? It wasn't five members 
in every generation?

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:26.400
That's what I thought it was...

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:28.460
Right, Princess?

00:13:28.460 --> 00:13:31.830
It's time for the show. 
Let's hurry and get ready.

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:34.150
What's wrong? Do you feel sick?

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:37.970
You've got us worried here. Talk to us.

00:13:37.970 --> 00:13:41.630
Just drop it, okay? 
Now go over the choreography.

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:43.630
Wh-What gives?

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:45.980
Gen, you should be using this 
time to go over the lyrics!

00:13:45.980 --> 00:13:48.230
Come on, Hululu, stop eating.

00:13:48.230 --> 00:13:50.840
We can't put on a satisfactory event like this.

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:54.430
Princess-san, are you okay? 
You're acting strange.

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:55.770
Calm down.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:14:02.510
Wait, are you self-conscious about 
not being in the other generations?

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:06.130
I can sing and dance circles around you.

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:07.490
Princess-san...

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:09.310
Do whatever you want!

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:13.440
What's her problem?

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:15.590
I'm sorry, I...

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:17.620
Margay-san, you didn't do anything wrong.

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:20.680
What do we do? We need to get 
out there or the audience will...

00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:21.430
Let's go after her.

00:14:21.430 --> 00:14:24.880
Leave her. She told us to 
do whatever we want.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:39.640
There she is!

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:42.020
She's right where Margay-san 
said she would be.

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:43.270
Princess!

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:46.740
Let's hurry back, okay? Everyone's waiting.

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:52.570
Come on, let's go! I'm sure 
the audience will wait for you.

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:56.310
I'm sorry to put you in this position 
when you're our guests.

00:14:56.310 --> 00:14:59.330
No, it's okay. What's the matter?

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:01.560
I give up.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:04.130
I'm afraid of the stage.

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:07.130
What happened? That's not like you.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:09.110
No, I've always felt this way.

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:11.720
There's never been a Royal Penguin 
in the group before.

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:14.470
How's the audience going to react to that?

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:18.770
It scares me. That's why 
I dragged the others into this.

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:22.860
But that's why you practiced so hard, isn't it?

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:24.860
Margay-san told us about it.

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:29.400
Since the group formed, you've pushed 
yourself twice as hard as the others.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:31.910
You pulled them this far.

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:38.330
Come on, let's go! 
Everyone's waiting for you!

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:40.220
Let me go!

00:15:40.220 --> 00:15:43.690
I was so mean to the others.

00:15:43.690 --> 00:15:45.590
I can't face them!

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:48.080
They can pull this off without me.

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:50.340
They're all real idols!

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:55.350
I bet they'd be really happy to hear that! 
Tell them face-to-face, okay?

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:58.470
Wow, what a big audience.

00:15:57.320 --> 00:15:59.520
So many.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:02.080
So here we go, huh?

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:04.900
Let's talk about how we got here.

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:07.870
She's the one who found all of us, right?

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:09.750
She sure startled me.

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:11.600
I was eating.

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:16.020
Completely out of nowhere, 
she said to me, "Be our leader!"

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:20.330
That girl is so abrupt, and bossy, too.

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:23.670
See? They're fine.

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:28.500
I knew it. They stuck with me 
even though they didn't want to.

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:30.560
But you know, once we gave it a try,

00:16:30.560 --> 00:16:33.080
the dancing and singing 
turned out to be tons of fun.

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:35.000
So did dancing for other people!

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:36.680
It's all thanks to Princess.

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:40.330
Margay told us that she pleaded 
with the professor again and again

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:42.890
so we could have an event like this...

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:46.930
And that she'd research the choreography 
and songs until late into the night,

00:16:46.930 --> 00:16:50.280
and practiced extra so she 
could teach them to us.

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:52.800
We can't start without Princess.

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:56.490
If we're going to surpass our predecessors, 
we need a new member.

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:59.950
You're watching, aren't you? 
Let's get this show on the road!

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:08.170
I can't watch this anymore. It's too clumsy.

00:17:12.160 --> 00:17:14.800
Without me...

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:15.930
Princess-san!

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:17.100
That's your cue!

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:21.110
You're hopeless!

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:25.340
Honestly! Emperor moves too stiffly.

00:17:25.340 --> 00:17:27.600
Gen's no good under pressure.

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:34.280
Rocker rushes too much, and who 
knows what goes on in Hululu's head?

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:38.170
But...

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:38.170
But...

00:17:38.170 --> 00:17:39.850
They've got a good vibe!

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:41.490
Time for our first song!

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:46.970
"Sky Dreamer"!

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:57.770
I can't fly through the sky,

00:17:57.770 --> 00:18:01.780
but I have dreams to be my wings!

00:18:01.780 --> 00:18:02.560
And that's why...

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.740
Drip drip, I'll work up a sweat!

00:18:04.740 --> 00:18:07.060
Gobble gobble, I'll grow up big!

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:11.220
And one day, I'll rule those skies!

00:18:11.220 --> 00:18:13.670
Crying, laughing,

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:14.920
Pop People Party!

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:15.740
PPP!

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:16.680
Push and shove?

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:17.800
Push and love.

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:18.950
Harsh environment?

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:20.030
I'm totally fine!

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:21.200
Hey, crowd in there.

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:22.280
You go away!

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:23.440
Squeeze, squeeze, squeeze, squeeze.

00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:24.620
Wow, how warm!

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:28.800
I'll leave my tracks in a brand new land

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:30.860
And hold my dreams tight.

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:34.880
The time to take off is now!

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:39.190
Even if my voice goes hoarse,

00:18:39.190 --> 00:18:43.300
I'll keep on singing.

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:44.310
And so I'll...

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:46.270
Zoom, zoom, travel the world!

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:48.520
Twinkle, twinkle, shine my light!

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:52.110
I'll go to the end of the world with you!

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:56.750
I can't fly through the sky,

00:18:56.750 --> 00:19:00.710
but I have dreams to be my wings!

00:19:00.710 --> 00:19:01.530
And that's why...

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:03.780
Drip, drip, I'll work up a sweat!

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:05.930
Gobble gobble, I'll grow up big!

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:09.750
And one day, I'll rule those skies!

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:12.610
Crying, laughing,

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:13.950
Pop People Party!

00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:14.290
PPP!

00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:20.340
But, man, you could've 
shown up a little sooner!

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:23.890
It was for dramatic effect! 
They loved it, didn't they?

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:26.940
It really is best when it's the five of us.

00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:29.480
This number is what makes us unique.

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:33.730
Huh? Weren't there always five penguin idols?

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:37.980
<i>Now</i> you ask?

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:38.670
Huh?

00:19:38.670 --> 00:19:41.560
Hululu-san, you weren't listening earlier?

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:42.800
That's so like you.

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:44.280
Huh? Huh?

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:45.580
It really is.

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:50.430
Now, time for the next song: 
"Welcome to Japari Park"!

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:55.460
Whew. That was a lot of dancing.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:56.960
I was so nervous.

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:58.710
We got a good reaction.

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:00.050
Good job out there!

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:02.280
You were incredible!

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:05.850
You were! With your tails 
bobbing back and forth, and...

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:09.570
Ahem! I want to thank you all, too.

00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:11.430
Now, Margay!

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:13.310
Y-Yes?!

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:18.070
Be our manager! Actually, you already are!

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:20.700
I'd love to!

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:28.600
I wanna have our next concert near the ocean.

00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:31.200
In that case, we should incorporate 
swimming into the performance.

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:32.500
Ocean?

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:37.500
You didn't know? The whole park's 
surrounded by an ocean.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:38.940
Really?

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:41.070
Really?

00:20:41.070 --> 00:20:43.090
Hey, you should know that.

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:45.510
So, you're looking for humans?

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:48.140
What kind of animal is that?

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:52.100
If I'm not mistaken, 
they were last seen at the harbor.

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:54.440
Huh? Really?!

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:58.580
But that was a long time ago. 
I doubt they're still there.

00:20:58.580 --> 00:21:00.310
Why are you searching for humans?

00:21:00.310 --> 00:21:05.490
I was told that I'm a human myself, 
so I'm looking for the Area where they lived.

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:09.540
You can't remember your territory? How awful.

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:13.850
No, I have a clue now. I'll go to the harbor!

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:16.220
Good luck. I'm sure you'll find something.

00:21:16.220 --> 00:21:17.330
Yeah!

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:18.940
That reminds me... Emperor-san,

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:21.650
did you say you've walked 
200 kilometers to your colony?

00:21:21.650 --> 00:21:24.910
That's right. I'd fast for 100 days, too.

00:21:24.910 --> 00:21:27.340
It was a hard life, if I say so myself...

00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:29.800
But you like that kind of thing.

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:31.990
They call that "masochism."

00:21:31.990 --> 00:21:35.280
Why are you only knowledgeable 
about things like that?

00:23:10.420 --> 00:23:12.500
Pass! Kick it, kick it!

00:23:12.500 --> 00:23:13.410
What?

00:23:13.410 --> 00:23:15.860
I don't understand, but leave this to m—

00:23:16.440 --> 00:23:18.450
I gotcha covered!

00:23:19.020 --> 00:23:20.330
Goal!

00:23:20.330 --> 00:23:22.750
Hey, wait, that's against the rules.

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:26.880
Long story short, she's a hat thief!

00:23:27.440 --> 00:23:28.540
I can't see it.

00:23:28.540 --> 00:23:30.140
Yeah, she's not that kind of girl.

00:23:30.140 --> 00:23:34.200
Such an evil act cannot be forgiven. 
The park is in grave danger!

00:23:34.960 --> 00:23:36.320
Sounds like a mix-up...

00:23:36.320 --> 00:23:39.370
Oh, it probably is.

00:23:39.370 --> 00:23:41.390
Not you, too!

00:23:41.790 --> 00:23:43.340
PPP Preview!

00:23:43.340 --> 00:23:45.530
This week, we're learning 
about the Ezo red fox.

00:23:45.530 --> 00:23:48.520
I guess they pretend to sleep 
to hunt their prey.

00:23:48.520 --> 00:23:50.980
So in PPP, who would be tastiest?

00:23:50.980 --> 00:23:51.890
I know.

00:23:51.890 --> 00:23:52.860
It's Hululu.

00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:53.610
What?!

00:23:53.610 --> 00:23:54.670
Is she? Really?

00:23:54.670 --> 00:23:56.380
Next time: "Snowy Mountains Area."
